{"id": "SGU_Episode_663", "title": "SGU Episode 663", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 663 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 663", "date": "March 24 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 3, "day": 24, "rogues": ["Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Cara Santa Maria", "Evan Bernstein"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dara_%C3%93_Briain", "quote": "\n It gets on my nerves when people say science doesn't know everything. Science knows it doesn't know everything, otherwise it would stop. Just because science doesn't know everything doesn't mean you can fill in the gaps with whatever fairy-tale appeals to you. \n", "quotee": "\n Dara \u00d3 Briain ", "quotee_title": " Irish comedian\n", "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-663", "episode_number": 663}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "Voice-over: You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n\n( links for Cara's mentions:\nP-22's decade in Griffith Park\nNPS Puma Profiles: P-022 )\n", "title": "Introduction, Nor\u2019easters, forest visits, \"Puma 22\"", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction, Nor\u2019easters, forest visits, \"Puma 22\""}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "Vagility[1][v 1]", "title": "What's the Word?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:06:51", "hour": 0, "minute": "6", "second": "51", "links": ["https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/blog/word-of-the-week/botanical-nerd-word-vagile/"], "title": "What's the Word?"}, "sections": [{"id": 2, "text": "_consider_using_block_quotes_for_emails_read_aloud_in_this_segment_", "metadata": {"speaker": "<unknown>"}}]}, {"id": 3, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 4, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 5, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "B"}}, {"id": 6, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_ab